live-boot-vyatta (0.12) trixie; urgency=medium

  * vyatta-union boots: allow persistence on the device that holds the live
    medium. Debian 13's live-boot blacklists it, so an installed image's
    persistence (on the same partition as its squashfs) was never found and
    every boot started from the default configuration.

